      "data": {
        "text": "**Defining the Provider**\n\nI've decided to use Google Cloud Text-to-Speech for synthesizing the text. I'll need to clearly identify this choice within the `synthesize_text.py` file itself to keep the code's dependence clear.\n\n\n**Implementing the Synthesis**\n\nOkay, I'm setting up the `synthesize_text.py` file now. I'm focusing on the code to synthesize text using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech. I'm importing the necessary library and setting up the client. Next, I will be defining the text, voice, and audio configurations. Then, it's just a matter of calling the synthesis method.\n\n\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789867745780,
          "start": 1789867743587
        },
        "type": "reasoning"
      },
      "id": "prt_0bc6e5963001gNldlem1LQ8pgB",
      "message_id": "msg_0bc6e542b001DaEW28CZtt7S2f",
      "session_id": "ses_f4391ac5bffeD4EWmyoCWOHjfX",
      "time_created": 1789867743587,
      "time_updated": 1789867745781
    },
    {
      "data": {
        "callID": "RBLkQXZCWXvL0Whn",
        "metadata": {
          "google": {
            "thoughtSignature": ""
          }
        },
        "state": {
          "input": {
            "content": "from google.cloud import texttospeech\nimport os\n\ndef synthesize_text(text):\n    \"\"\"Synthesizes plain text to an audio byte stream using Google Cloud Text-to-Speech.\"\"\"\n\n    # Set up Google Cloud credentials (if not already set via environment variables)\n    # os.environ[\"GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS\"] = \"path/to/your/credentials.json\"\n\n    client = texttospeech.TextToSpeechClient()\n\n    input_text = textophen.SynthesisInput(text=text)\n\n    # Select the voice and audio file type\n    voice = texttospeech.VoiceSelectionParams(\n        language_code=\"en-US\",\n        name=\"en-US-Standard-C\",  # Example voice\n        ssml_gender=texttospeech.SsmlVoiceGender.NEUTRAL,\n    )\n\n    audio_config = texttospeech.AudioConfig(\n        audio_encoding=texttospeech.AudioEncoding.MP3\n    )\n\n    response = client.synthesize_speech(\n        request={\"input\": input_text, \"voice\": voice, \"audio_config\": audio_config}\n    )\n\n    # The audio content is binary. You can save it to a file or stream it.\n    return response.audio_content\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    text_to_synthesize = \"Hello, this is a test of the Google Cloud Text-to-Speech API.\"\n    audio_bytes = synthesize_text(text_to_synthesize)\n\n    with open(\"output.mp3\", \"wb\") as out:\n        out.write(audio_bytes)\n        print('Audio content written to file \"output.mp3\"')\n",
            "filePath": "synthesize_text.py"
          },
